From: winglm port
Subject: [PATCH] monitor-manager: announce a monitor only once

on_monitor_configured() emitted 'monitor-added' before disconnecting from
the monitor's 'configured' signal. The lockscreen manager reacts to
'monitor-added' by mapping a lock shield, and mapping a layer surface runs
a Wayland roundtrip. For a hotplugged output that roundtrip delivers the
xdg-output name and position plus the next wl_output.done, so the monitor
is 'configured' again and announced a second time from within the first
emission: the output ends up with two lock shields stacked on each other.

Disconnect before emitting.
---
--- a/src/monitor-manager.c	2026-11-16 03:22:13.059386089 +0400
+++ b/src/monitor-manager.c	2026-11-16 03:22:13.073408544 +0400
@@ -970,11 +970,15 @@
   g_return_if_fail (PHOSH_IS_MONITOR_MANAGER (self));
   g_return_if_fail (PHOSH_IS_MONITOR (monitor));
 
+  /* Disconnect first: a handler of 'monitor-added' can run a Wayland
+   * roundtrip (mapping a layer surface does) that delivers the output's
+   * next 'done' and so 'configured' again while we're still in here,
+   * announcing the same monitor twice */
+  g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_data (monitor, self);
+
   g_signal_emit (self, signals[SIGNAL_MONITOR_ADDED], 0, monitor);
   g_object_notify_by_pspec (G_OBJECT (self), props[PROP_N_MONITORS]);
 
-  g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_data (monitor, self);
-
   /* A monitor reconfiguration via DBus might have a pending primary monitor change */
   if (self->pending_primary) {
     PhoshMonitor *primary_monitor;
